# Validation 5: a Magician wish. With the Magician on (03) and the wish box on the Magician (04), a wish typed into the
# watch goes to the wish model (Opus 5.5 on the Claude subscription, through Claude Code), which builds something new from scratch:
# no ready-made part. Here it is asked for a creature nobody has made before, so the Apprentice has no tile for it.
@intent A typed wish goes to the Magician on the Claude subscription, which makes a new creature that appears in the world

@step a clear stage
gamemode creative
time set noon
weather clear
gamerule advance_time false
gamerule spawn_mobs false
execute if entity @e[type=!minecraft:player] run kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 10

@step wish for something new, on the watch
@key key.use
@expect screen /make a wish/ within 10s
# Moddy puts an idea in the box; @type replaces it with the wish.
@type "a small teal hedgehog with glowing orange spikes that rolls into a ball when it is scared"
@wait 1s
@shot the-wish-typed
@click button "Make my wish"
# While it works, the action bar shows what it is doing and a running timer: "🏗 🔧 Reshaping it… (30s)".
@expect actionbar /\([0-9]+s\)/ within 90s
@shot the-magician-at-work

@step the wish comes true
# The wish model plans, builds and checks it: a few minutes is normal.
@expect chat /is ready|came true|all done/ within 600s
@wait 3s
@shot the-wish-made

@step the creature is in the world
@repeat 15 until execute if entity @e[tag=wishmob]
@wait 1s
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @e[tag=wishmob]
